cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "quantum-solar: an exactly-solved battery-scheduling instance for QAOA method work, with a slack-free encoding"
authors:
  - family-names: Amissah
    given-names: Austin
    website: "https://amissah.net"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-08-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/austinamissah/quantum-solar"
url: "https://github.com/austinamissah/quantum-solar"
keywords:
  - QAOA
  - quantum optimization
  - QUBO
  - constraint encoding
  - battery scheduling
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  A home solar-battery scheduling problem solved exactly on a real Colorado
  year (Golden, CO: PVWatts generation, Xcel URDB prices, NREL ResStock load),
  used as a checkable instance for QAOA method work. Three results: a
  slack-free checkpoint encoding whose zero-penalty assignments are all
  provably feasible; a measured penalty-weight scale and the reproducibility
  cost of overshooting it; and in-constraint probability used as a post-hoc
  selector among tuning restarts. Only the first appears to be new, on a
  prior-art scan whose limits are recorded in docs/FINDINGS.md; the other two
  are rediscoveries, kept for their measurements. Six small pre-registered
  hardware runs on ibm_fez back the device-level claims. Not a claim of
  quantum advantage: an exact dynamic program solves every instance here in
  microseconds.
